<h2>What stays the same everywhere we work</h2>
<p>Wherever your property is located, the process is the same: a Free Claim Review, a written contract with fees disclosed before any work begins, a thorough inspection, careful documentation, and ongoing communication with your insurer. Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement, and you may rescind the contract within 72 hours of signing.</p>
<p>Southeast Texas also shares a few insurance realities. Standard homeowners and commercial policies generally exclude flood, including storm surge and rising water, so flood losses go to an NFIP or private flood policy. Many policies carry separate hurricane or wind/hail deductibles calculated as a percentage of the dwelling limit; try the <a href="/hurricane-deductible-calculator/">hurricane deductible calculator</a>. And high humidity means water damage can lead to mold quickly. Our <a href="/services/flood-damage-claims/">flood damage claims</a> and <a href="/services/storm-damage-claims/">storm damage claims</a> pages explain more.</p>
